Title: The Ruins of Meroe
Order: 13
Production Code: 1x13

EXT. MEROE - PYRAMID FIELD - DAY

AMB: wind over eighty ruined pyramids, distant Arab workers

The expedition excavates in earnest. [[Charlie Vance]] mounts the tallest pyramid to declaim, badly, at his companions; [[Professor Stone]] catalogs golden plates, a statue of Candace on a golden chariot flanked by silver serpents. Treasure enough is found and shipped home to satisfy the expedition's backers, though the Sphinx-head door the parchment described won't move for any tool they own.

[[Jim Titus]] is kept at a careful distance now, set to guard the camp's stores rather than travel with [[Reuel Briggs]] directly — a quiet decision both Reuel and Charlie have made without needing to say why aloud.

Reuel grows more withdrawn by the week, pacing the camp at night, waiting on a mail that keeps not coming.

CHARLIE VANCE
You ought not, Briggs. Come, shake off that sadness before it makes an end of you.

REUEL BRIGGS
(distant)
I've begun to regret the leopard missed.

At dusk, Ababdis arrives at last with the long-delayed mail from Cairo.
